### How data flows

- `useKitAppSelection()` gives selected IDs by kind (`types`, `designs`, `ports`, `tags`, `files`, etc).
- Those IDs are set by table/interaction handlers (`setSelectionAction({...})`).
- Detail components resolve IDs against the live `kit` object (`useKit()`), e.g. `kit.types.find(...)`, `kit.designs.find(...)`.
- Sections are registered dynamically via `addSection("details", ...)`; panel renders `usePanelSections("details")`.

### What shows up in the Details panel (Kit app)

- **Always shown:** Kit section (`KitSection`) at order 100.
- **When one kind is selected:** one of  
  - Design details (`KitDesignSection`)  
  - Type details (`TypeSection`)  
  - Port details (`PortSection`)  
  - Tag details (`TagSection`)  
  - File details (`FileSection`)  
  - Folder details (`FolderSection`)
- **When multiple kinds are selected at once:** `MultipleArtifactsSection` summary string (“X types, Y designs, ...”).

### Exact fields shown

Kit fields (editable, lazy write to store via `kitDataSource.change(...)`):

