## Exactly Where Design Data Lives

### 1) Runtime source of truth (for UI)
Design detail hooks read from **kit store snapshot** (`kitStore.getSnapshot().kit`), then pick the scoped design/piece/connection:

```7291:7344:compose/sketchpad/index.tsx
function useKitSnapshot(): Kit | null {
  const kitStore = useKitStore() as KitStore | null;
  // ...
  return useSyncExternalStore(subscribe, getSnapshot); // getSnapshot().kit
}

export function useDesign<T = Design>(selector?: (design: Design) => T, deep?: boolean, id?: string): T | Design | null {
  const designGuid = useDesignScope()?.guid ?? id;
  const kit = useKitSnapshot();
  const design = kit.designs?.find((d) => d.guid === designGuid) ?? null;
  return selector ? selector(design) : design;
}
```

So data is under:
- `kit.designs[]`
- each design has `pieces[]` and `connections[]`

### 2) Mutation model
Design app commands emit a **`kitDiff`** against `context.design.guid`. That means edits are applied into the kit’s design object.

```27660:27824:compose/sketchpad/index.tsx
"compose.designApp.addPiece": (...) => ({
  kitDiff: { designs: { updated: [{ design: { guid: context.design.guid }, diff: { pieces: { added: [piece] } } }] } }
}),
"compose.designApp.addConnection": (...) => ({
  kitDiff: { designs: { updated: [{ design: { guid: context.design.guid }, diff: { connections: { added: [connection] } } }] } }
}),
"compose.designApp.updatePiece": (...) => ({
  kitDiff: { designs: { updated: [{ design: { guid: context.design.guid }, diff: { pieces: { updated: [{ piece: { guid: pieceGuid }, diff: pieceDiff }] } } }] } }
}),
```

