## Where The Tree Structure Comes From

There are **two layers** of tree structure:

1. **Panel section tree** (top-level sections in right panel)  
   Comes from `addSection("details", ...)`, then rendered by `PanelTabContent`:

```24138:24154:compose/sketchpad/index.tsx
const sortedSections = [...sections].sort((a, b) => (a.order || 0) - (b.order || 0));
const treeSections = sortedSections.map((section) => ({ id: section.id, content: section.content() }));
<Tree sections={treeSections} />
```

2. **Nested tree inside each section**  
   Built explicitly with `TreeItem` + `TreeRow` in section components:
   - piece subtree (`pieceInfo`, `attributes`, `center`, `plane`, `parentConnection`)
   - connection subtree (`connecting`, `connected`, `translation`, `orientation`, `diagram`)

```32361:32593:compose/sketchpad/index.tsx
<TreeItem id="...piece.pieceInfo">
  <TreeRow>...</TreeRow>
  <TreeItem id="...piece.attributes">...</TreeItem>
  <TreeItem id="...piece.center">...</TreeItem>
  <TreeItem id="...piece.plane">...</TreeItem>
</TreeItem>
```

```32742:32948:compose/sketchpad/index.tsx
<TreeItem id="...connection.connecting">...</TreeItem>
<TreeItem id="...connection.connected">...</TreeItem>
<TreeItem id="...connection.translation">...</TreeItem>
<TreeItem id="...connection.orientation">...</TreeItem>
<TreeItem id="...connection.diagram">...</TreeItem>
```

So the tree is not auto-inferred from schema; it is manually composed from:
- current selection
- explicit `TreeItem` nesting in each details component.
